.TH MOUNT.OCSFS 8 "March 2026" "ocsfs 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
mount.ocsfs \- mount helper for OCSFS filesystems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mount.ocsfs
.I device
.I mount\-point
[\fB\-o\fR \fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mount.ocsfs
is a mount helper invoked automatically by
.BR mount (8)
when using the
.B \-t ocsfs
filesystem type. It performs pre-mount validation:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Validates the device contains an OCSFS superblock (via ocsfs\-tool)
.IP \(bu 2
Loads the ocsfs kernel module if not already loaded
.IP \(bu 2
Delegates to the kernel mount(2) system call
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o " " \fIoptions\fR
Comma-separated mount options passed through to the kernel.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
mount \-t ocsfs /dev/mapper/mpath\-3600508b... /mnt/ocsfs
.RE
.PP
Or via /etc/fstab:
.PP
.RS 4
/dev/mapper/mpath\-3600508b... /mnt/pve/fc\-shared ocsfs defaults,_netdev 0 0
.RE
.PP
Note: use
.B _netdev
for SAN devices to ensure the mount waits for the storage network.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/sbin/mount.ocsfs
The mount helper binary.
.TP
.B /usr/sbin/ocsfs\-tool
Used for superblock validation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mount (8),
.BR mkfs.ocsfs (8),
.BR ocsfs\-tool (8),
.BR ocsfs\-defrag (8)
